WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.949
Can't you just look at the AI's outputs and see if they're good? For ten outputs, sure. For the ten thousand your feature produces every day — not a chance.

00:08.949 --> 00:18.783
Eyeballing doesn't scale, it isn't repeatable, and it misses the slow drift — the quality that erodes a little each week until a customer notices it before you do.

00:18.783 --> 00:27.039
So I make it systematic: a scored rubric, run automatically, on every change. The same standard, every time, at any volume.

00:27.039 --> 00:32.647
Human judgment sets the standard. The system enforces it — at a scale no human can.

00:32.647 --> 00:35.787
Stop spot-checking. Start measuring. Let's talk.

